  "lineage": "Duet song-and-dance theatre of northeast China (Liaoning, Jilin and Heilongjiang), in which a clown-role man and a dan-role woman sing, talk, joke and dance with fans and handkerchiefs; it entered China's national intangible heritage list in 2006 and reached national audiences through television and commercial theatres. The banhu fiddle leads, with suona, while the performers snap hand-held clappers (yuzi and bamboo boards; the paiban card in its kuaiban form stands in).",
